# Lab 3: Cloud Issue Tracker Architecture

## 1. Application Goal
To transition the Cloud Issue Tracker into a structured three-layer architecture separating client presentation, REST routing/validation, and persistent data storage.

## 2. Functional Scope
1. Create an issue.
2. View all issues.
3. Change an issue status.

## 3. Request Flow

### CREATE ISSUE
User -> Frontend form -> POST /api/issues -> API validation -> Data layer -> Render created issue (201 Created + JSON)

### VIEW ISSUES
Page load -> GET /api/issues -> API -> Data layer -> Render list (200 OK + JSON array)

### CHANGE STATUS
Button -> PATCH /api/issues/{id}/status -> API validation -> Data layer -> Re-render issue (200 OK + updated JSON)

